# The docs: GitBook, synced from docs/ on main through gitbook-docs.yaml. GitBook files each page under its
# SUMMARY.md group, not under its repo path: docs/agents/x.md is served at /for-agents/x, docs/concepts/x.md at
# /how-a-verdict-is-made/x, and docs/measured.md at /evidence/measured. So every page is mapped one to one; a bare
# :splat sent /docs/measured to a GitBook 404 (checked live 2026-11-20).
# The host is the GitBook address, not docs.djzs.ai: the custom domain runs on a GitBook trial (7 days from
# 2026-11-20). While the domain is active, GitBook forwards this address to docs.djzs.ai with the path kept; if
# the trial lapses, this address keeps serving. If the paid plan is kept, swap the host for https://docs.djzs.ai.
# Static rules first, the one dynamic fallback last (Cloudflare: static redirects before dynamic ones).
/docs https://djzsx.gitbook.io/djzs.ai/ 302
